{
  "$note": "kwwk's corrections to pi-mono's catalog, laid over it by kwwk-generate-models. Objects merge key by key, other values replace, null removes. Say why and when beside each group.",
  "kimi-coding": {
    "$note": "Kimi's coding endpoint returns thinking with an empty signature and refuses a replay that drops it (kwwk #183, 2026-10-11); k3-256k is priced, not free.",
    "k3-256k": {
      "compat": {
        "allowEmptySignature": true
      },
      "cost": {
        "input": 3,
        "output": 15,
        "cacheRead": 0.3
      }
    },
    "kimi-for-coding-highspeed": {
      "compat": {
        "allowEmptySignature": true
      }
    }
  },
  "github-copilot": {
    "$note": "Copilot's own limits and list, read from GET api.githubcopilot.com/models with a signed-in account on 2026-10-13. pi-mono carries each vendor's native window (1M for most), which Copilot does not give: a session would overflow long before kwwk thought to compact. contextWindow is Copilot's max_prompt_tokens + max_output_tokens (never above its max_context_window_tokens), since kwwk budgets a prompt as the window less the output reserve. A null is a model Copilot no longer lists.",
